<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Unna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Unna is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the eastern edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhr">Ruhr</a>, east of Dortmund. A town of the County of the Mark and a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>, it prospered from the salt works of nearby Königsborn and from trade on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellweg">Hellweg</a> road. It later became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>-mining and commuter town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/unna.jpg" alt="Unna" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Smial on de.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unna_Alter_Markt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
